# nano(1)

## NAME

nano - a small text editor

## SYNOPSIS

    nano [+LINE[,COLUMN]] [FILE]

## DESCRIPTION

Edits a text file on the terminal, in the style of GNU nano. The key list is shown at the bottom of the screen. Standard input and output must be a terminal.

## KEYS

- `Ctrl+G, F1`: help
- `Ctrl+X`: exit (asks to save changes)
- `Ctrl+O`: write to a file
- `Ctrl+S`: save
- `Ctrl+W`: search
- `Ctrl+K, Ctrl+U`: cut and paste lines
- `Ctrl+_`: go to a line
- `Ctrl+C`: show the cursor position

